---
import DeepDiveLayout from '../../layouts/DeepDiveLayout.astro';
---

<DeepDiveLayout
  title="Deep Dive into Barrel Path"
  pillar="Barrel Path"
  chapterNumber="04"
  nextTitle="Adjustability"
  nextHref="/learn/adjustability"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Quick Recap</h2>

    <p>
      Barrel path is the natural result of an efficient firing sequence.
    </p>

    <p>
      The hitter should not manipulate the barrel into the hitting zone.
    </p>

    <p>
      When the body moves efficiently, the barrel naturally arrives on plane,
      enters the zone, stays through contact, and releases afterward.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Before We Begin</h2>

    <p>
      Barrel path is one of the most debated topics in modern hitting.
    </p>

    <p>
      Many hitters spend countless hours trying to place the barrel in the
      perfect position.
    </p>

    <p>
      Launch Baseball takes a different approach.
    </p>

    <p>
      We don't teach hitters to move the barrel.
    </p>

    <p>
      We teach hitters to move their body correctly and allow the barrel to
      respond naturally.
    </p>

    <p class="callout">
      The barrel is a passenger, not the driver.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What We Want From the Barrel</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Enter the hitting zone naturally.</li>
      <li>Stay through the zone as long as possible.</li>
      <li>Meet the baseball with a square barrel.</li>
      <li>Release naturally after contact.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      A quality barrel path should require very little conscious manipulation.
    </p>

    <p class="callout">
      Good sequence creates good barrel path.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Trust the Sequence</h2>

    <p>
      The hitter has already completed the load.
    </p>

    <p>
      The lower half has fired.
    </p>

    <p>
      The torso has accelerated.
    </p>

    <p>
      The hands have fired toward the contact position.
    </p>

    <p>
      At this point, the barrel should simply respond to the movement that has
      already taken place.
    </p>

    <p>
      Trying to steer, force, or guide the barrel often creates compensations
      that reduce consistency.
    </p>

    <p class="callout">
      Fire the hands to the contact position. Trust the barrel to arrive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      The location of contact changes with pitch location.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Inside pitches are contacted farther in front.</li>
      <li>Middle pitches are contacted near the front foot.</li>
      <li>Outside pitches travel deeper before contact.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The body adjusts where contact occurs.
    </p>

    <p>
      The hitter should not manipulate the barrel to create those adjustments.
    </p>
  </section>

<section>
  <h2>Drills</h2>

  <div class="drill-grid">

    <article class="drill-card">
      <h3>Contact Position Holds</h3>
      <p>
        Learn exactly what an efficient contact position looks and feels like
        on inside, middle, and outside pitches.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="drill-card">
      <h3>Barrel Through Contact</h3>
      <p>
        Feel the barrel continue naturally through the contact position instead
        of stopping, steering, or rolling over.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="drill-card">
      <h3>One-Hand Swings</h3>
      <p>
        Reinforce natural barrel delivery while exposing unnecessary
        manipulation of the barrel.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="drill-card">
      <h3>Soft Toss</h3>
      <p>
        Work middle, inside, outside, high, and low locations while maintaining
        the same sequence and allowing contact to move naturally.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="drill-card">
      <h3>Broomstick Tee Work</h3>
      <p>
        Precision training that immediately exposes flaws in barrel path and
        contact position.
      </p>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

  <section>
    <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Trying to steer the barrel.</li>
      <li>Pushing the hands away from the body.</li>
      <li>Manipulating the barrel before contact.</li>
      <li>Releasing the hands too early.</li>
      <li>Confusing barrel movement with body movement.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="callout">
      The body creates the barrel path.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Self Evaluation</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Am I trying to move the barrel?</li>
      <li>Do my hands fire directly toward contact?</li>
      <li>Does the barrel enter naturally?</li>
      <li>Does the barrel stay through the zone?</li>
      <li>Do I release only after contact?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

</DeepDiveLayout>